NV_PK(10,{"1653":"","work began in 1653 a year after the guo huaiyi uprising":"","after the guo huaiyi uprising in 1652 they wanted a strong base on land":"","koxinga's army surrounded the fort and it surrendered in 1661":"","the fleet of 1661":"","the red bricks under your feet were laid by the dutch in the 1650s":"","in 1661 koxinga took this fort and made it his government office":"","in 1653 the dutch east india company began building fort provintia at sakam":"","in 1625 the dutch traded 15 bolts of cloth to the siraya people for land at sakam":"","the 1652 uprising":"","after the guo huaiyi uprising in 1652 the dutch wanted a strong fort on land":"","work began in 1653 locals called it the red hair tower":"","in 1661 koxinga's army arrived and fort provintia was the first to surrender":"","in spring 1661 koxinga's fleet sailed into the taijiang inner sea":"","surrounded the dutch officer valentyn surrendered the fort in 1661":"","fort zeelandia in anping held out for about nine months until early 1662":"","after the lin shuangwen uprising emperor qianlong wrote texts in 1788 carved in chinese and manchu":"","legend says one bixi fell into the sea at anping fishermen found it in 1911":"","a repair finished in 1944 uncovered the old dutch gate and bastion":""});